&lt;div class=&quot;image-container aligncenter&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://scp-sandbox-3.wdfiles.com/local--files/barredowl/scp.png&quot; width=&quot;500px&quot; alt=&quot;scp.png&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WARNING:&lt;/strong&gt; These author commentaries are extremely laden with spoilers. Proceed with care.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;▶&amp;nbsp;COMMENTARY&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;▷&amp;nbsp;COMMENTARY&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My first published SCP. To be honest, I&#039;m immensely proud with how it turned out, especially for my first article, and I was extremely happy when I saw how much it resonated with some people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The inspiration for this article stemmed from a less-than-favorable trip to an old childhood park of mine. I was mostly expecting to be flooded with nostalgic warmth and happiness while traveling through it, but instead I accidentally uprooted a lot of bad memories (kids being shitty to me, other personal stuff). That was really the impetus for making this &amp;#8212; I wanted to tell a story which related to my own experiences during elementary school and spin it into a weird, shape-shifting anomaly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The original drafts for this SCP actually included a subplot about a person of interest who made the park to perform a ritual in a nearby hotel to resurrect the memory of their dead friend and &amp;#8212; yeah, I ditched that. In those earlier drafts Poplar was less fleshed-out, and everything was in audio format, so you constantly had characters describing to other characters what happened to Poplar. That got real messy real quick, so I decided to keep it in video format.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of the last structural changes I made to this was including the interview. Originally, I thought that ending the article at the exploration log would make the ending suspenseful. But then I found that it was way too open-ended of an&amp;#8230; ending to be emotionally satisfying; hence, the interview. I&#039;m actually the most proud of the interview, and I really think it helps give the piece some emotional depth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My critters were incredibly helpful in bringing fruition to this article, so I&#039;ll list their lovely names here:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
